
# db/*.sql migration files embed self-referential md5 fingerprints of their own
# function source text (see db/push_subscriptions_draft.sql, which hashes
# pg_proc.prosrc for functions defined in the same file, including its own
# multi-line function body). Those fingerprints are hardcoded against LF text.
# On Windows checkouts, the repo-wide core.autocrlf=true setting rewrites these
# files to CRLF, which changes the hashed source text and breaks the fixtures'
# preflight self-checks (see tests/sql/pglite-push-subscriptions.mjs and
# tests/sql/pglite-employment-status-access-block.mjs, which both apply
# db/push_subscriptions_draft.sql). Force LF regardless of core.autocrlf so the
# checked-out bytes match what the fingerprints were computed against.
db/*.sql text eol=lf

# 예외: 운영에 적용된 Task 8 함수 본문이 CRLF로 기록돼 있어 해시 08d9fa62와
# 일치시키기 위함 (db/attendance_owner_chief_gate_patch.sql의
# EXPECTED_NEW_FUNCTION_PROSRC_MD5는 CRLF 기준으로 고정된 운영 실측값).
db/attendance_owner_chief_gate_patch.sql text eol=crlf
